# Small scenes in the catacombs' named crypts (Dungeon Expansion Plan C1; docs/regions/castle_ravenloft_catacombs.md §14).
# Lines drafted by Gemini through the ai-bridge, trimmed by hand (docs/story/gemini_drafts/castle_crypts/).

# Saint Markovia's thighbone (prop cat_markovia_bone, crypt 6 in the Lesser Vaults). The darts guard it.
# The thighbone is the item `saint_markovias_thighbone` (castle-artifacts, Dungeon Expansion Plan I1, docs/story/castle_artifacts.md):
# lifting it from the lid gives it to the party, once.

~ markovia_bone
narrate examine:cat_markovia_bone
if flag.cat_markovia_bone_lifted
-> END
endif
* Lift the thighbone from the lid. -> lift
* Leave the relic where it lies. -> END

~ lift
set cat_markovia_bone_lifted
give saint_markovias_thighbone
Narrator: As you lift the linen from the stone, the air grows cold. A pale woman in a worn apron stands beside you, her hands folded and still.
Narrator: "You have come a long way through the dark, children, and my rest was long. Take what remains of me where it is needed, and let it mend what this castle has torn."
-> END

# The Baron's brown mold (prop cat_eisglaze_mold, crypt 29). Fire clears it, and the cold trap with it.
~ eisglaze_mold
narrate examine:cat_eisglaze_mold
if flag.cat_eisglaze_mold_burnt
-> END
endif
* [if item:torch or item:oil or item:alchemists_fire] Hold fire to the slab and burn the mold away. -> burn
* Step back and leave the mold be. -> END

~ burn
set cat_eisglaze_mold_burnt
Narrator: The brown velvet curls and blackens without a sound as your flame touches it. All at once, the bitter chill lets go of your lungs.
-> END

# Sir Klutz Tripalotsky (prop cat_klutz_sword, crypt 33). Pull the sword and his ghost offers to fight one battle at
# the party's side (a guest who leaves once that fight ends: data/npcs/sir_klutz.json `leaves_after_fight`).
~ klutz_sword
narrate examine:cat_klutz_sword
if flag.cat_klutz_freed
-> END
endif
* Draw the longsword free from the dented breastplate. -> pull
* Leave the blade wedged where it is. -> END

~ pull
set cat_klutz_freed
Narrator: A tall ghost in bright mail steps out of the stone, bows with great dignity, and catches his left spur squarely on the threshold.
sir_klutz: My earnest thanks for the iron, friends, and my apologies in advance if I tread upon your cloaks. I have one good battle left in me, if you will have me.
* Come with us. We would be glad of your sword. -> join
* Your wars are done, sir. Rest now. -> rest
* We should put the sword back where it was. -> sword_back

~ join
sir_klutz: Splendid! Lead on, and pray stand a pace to my right, as my scabbard has a wicked habit of swinging when I turn.
join sir_klutz
-> END

~ rest
sir_klutz: Ah. Quite right, of course; a wise captain keeps his ranks tidy. I shall just lie back down here and try not to rattle.
-> END

~ sword_back
sir_klutz: Oh, do not mind on my account. It went in between the fourth and fifth ribs when my heel met the stair, and truthfully, I had grown used to the draught.
-> rest
